📓 Jupyter Notebook Lab – Uses

1. Data Preprocessing

Clean the data.
Handle missing values.
Remove duplicate data.
Convert data into a suitable format for Machine Learning.
Raw Data → Cleaned Data

=============

2. Model Training

Train the Machine Learning model using prepared data.

Examples:
Linear Regression
Decision Tree
Random Forest
Deep Learning models

Training Data → ML Model Training


==========

3. Model Building

Create and configure the ML model.
Select algorithms.
Define model parameters.
Develop the model architecture.

Data + Algorithm → Build Model

========

4. Model Evaluation

Check how well the trained model performs.

Use metrics such as:
Accuracy
Precision
Recall
RMSE

Trained Model → Performance Check

=========

5. Deployment
Deploy the trained model for real-world use.
